cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Murmr in your research, academic work, or software projects, please cite it as below."
title: "Murmr: Zero-Trust End-to-End Encrypted Messaging with Acoustic Out-of-Band Key Exchange"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Sirvent Jiménez"
    given-names: "Pablo"
    email: "pablo@purebyte.ai"
    affiliation: "Universitat Oberta de Catalunya (UOC)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sirventai/murmr-app"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-05-08
abstract: >-
  Murmr is a cross-platform (Android, iOS, Desktop) end-to-end encrypted
  messaging application developed as a Final Degree Project (Trabajo de Fin
  de Grado - TFG) in Computer Engineering at the Universitat Oberta de
  Catalunya (UOC). It introduces an innovative physical acoustic channel
  operating at near-ultrasonic frequencies (15-19 kHz) for out-of-band (OOB)
  cryptographic key exchange, fully mitigating Trust-On-First-Use (TOFU)
  risks and eliminating reliance on central key directories. Subsequent
  communication uses AES-256-GCM authenticated encryption routed through
  a zero-knowledge relay server.
keywords:
  - end-to-end encryption
  - acoustic key exchange
  - out-of-band authentication
  - near-ultrasound
  - kotlin multiplatform
  - compose multiplatform
  - zero-knowledge
  - computer engineering
  - uoc tfg
